    "concept": {
      "movement": "A low, deliberate alternating-tripod stalk with six large walking limbs, separate front palps and a steady crystal abdomen. The faster skitter increases reach and cadence without bouncing the body.",
      "attack": "The legs brace as the body coils briefly, then drives the face and palps straight forward in a venomous bite thrust. The small fangs close inward and the spider recovers to its stance.",
      "death": "The crystal body sinks onto the ground while the six legs curl inward in a staggered release; the front palps relax, then the corpse holds still."
    },
